    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0101" n="31" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg31"/>

                <head>No. 20.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Baron Schaeffer to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-11-21"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 21, 1883</date>.
                        (Received November 22.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter dated 13th instant, with respect to the unfortunate affairs of
                    the two Hungarian ships, Mimi P. and Ararat, in Philadelphia.</p>
                <p>I cannot but express my sincerest thanks for the compliance with my request by
                    which you enable me to give to my Government a detailed reply, so urgently asked
                    for by them.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>SCHAEFFER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
